60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I vote for Option B. It balances psychological comfort with a predictable budget, avoiding the ""coat in the living room"" scenario.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I'm worried about the work involved in all of these, but B seems like the least amount of monthly effort. I'll go with B.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I wanted C for fairness, but the cost and the effort Mio mentioned make it impractical. I'll vote for B to stop the monthly friction.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Option B solves the volatility of the winter bills and avoids the high upfront cost of Option C. It is the most rational choice.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"If everyone likes B and it stops the fighting, then I like it too. I vote for B.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have a rare moment of total consensus.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,Yay! No more forty-minute math sessions every single month!,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"As long as we are honest during the year-end settlement, this should work.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,Agreed. It provides the stability I need without an immediate financial burden.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,I'm just happy we're all agreeing.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
